{"id": "86258", "name": "שברים חלקיים – גורם לינארי וגורם לינארי בריבוע (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Express</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}} \\]</p><p>as a sum of partial fractions.</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> A linear factor and a repeated linear factor: write the form, multiply by the denominator and substitute convenient values of x.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The form</b><br>The basic partial fraction information is:<div style=\"background:#FFF8E6;border:1px solid #E8D29A;border-radius:10px;padding:10px 14px;margin:12px 0\"><b>Rules of partial fractions.</b> If the degree of the numerator is at least the degree of the denominator, divide first. Then each factor of the denominator gives terms:<ul style=\"margin:6px 0\"><li>a linear factor \\(ax+b\\): \\(\\dfrac{A}{ax+b}\\);</li><li>a repeated linear factor \\((ax+b)^2\\): \\(\\dfrac{A}{ax+b}+\\dfrac{B}{(ax+b)^2}\\);</li><li>an irreducible quadratic factor \\(ax^2+bx+c\\): \\(\\dfrac{Ax+B}{ax^2+bx+c}\\).</li></ul></div>So, given<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}}=\\frac{A}{{CT:1}} + \\frac{B}{{CT:2}} + \\frac{C}{{CT:3}}, \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Finding the constants</b><br>then multiplying through by the denominator {{CT:4}} we have that<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:5}} = {{CT:6}} + {{CT:7}}+{{CT:8}}. \\]</p>Setting \\(x = {{CT:9}}\\) we see that \\(A = {{CT:10}}\\) and letting \\(x = {{CT:11}}\\) we find that \\(C = {{CT:12}}\\). Putting \\(x = 0\\) we can also see that \\(B = {{CT:13}}\\).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — The answer</b><br>Therefore<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}}={{CT:14}}. \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">You may have made a common error.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "PartFrac", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "answer", "testoptions": "x", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "ALG-RPF-TRUE", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "ALG-RPF-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "answer", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "ALG-RPF-1-FALSE", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "ALG-RPF-2-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "EqualComAss", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "f", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "NO-CHANGE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p>This seems to be the same expression that you started with.</p></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "NOT-PARTIAL", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p>Although your expression is algebraically equal to the correct answer, it is not in partial fractions form.</p></div>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["Aden2_squared", "Aval", "Bden1_den2", "Bval", "Cden1", "Cval", "a", "answer", "b", "c", "c_minus_d", "d", "den", "den1", "den2", "den2_squared", "f", "mag_b", "mag_d", "mc", "md", "numerat", "sign_b", "sign_d"], "nvariants": 50}